# that computes every score with the Triton kernel's own instruction sequence, read from its PTX: the mma K order of
# Triton's kWidth-4 dot layout, the epilogue's roundings, the head sum's order. A CTA of 8 rows converts each 64-pool
# FP8 key tile once for all of them. Every score is the Triton kernel's bit for bit. FP8 caches with 32 indexer heads of
# 128 only (the indexer is replicated: TP=2 and TP=3 alike). The extension (tensorfold_glm_scores_v1) is built / loaded
# by decode.Engine's constructor, before any request; loaded lazily, a fresh image built it at its first long prompt
# while every stream waited. TF_GLM_SCORES_CUDA=0: the Triton kernel, which also serves (logged once) under another
# Triton release than the one whose PTX the kernel reproduces (sparse.TRITON_PTX, 3.7) and when the extension fails to
# build or load. Applies after patch 0101 (both edit _select_prompt). tools/prompt_scores_check.py.

